{"time": "2026-06-08T22:50:37", "event": "post_written", "user_id": "c_graph_drift_g001_a03_4224604e_007", "post_id": "zjxngoz", "subreddit": "InternationalNews", "content": "Every time someone talks about the 'day after' in Gaza, the proposals are incredibly vague. We hear about 'international peacekeeping forces' or a 'revitalized Palestinian Authority' taking over, but nobody actually names which countries are going to step up and put boots on the ground. It just feels like wishful thinking."}
{"time": "2026-06-08T22:50:37", "event": "post_written", "user_id": "c_graph_drift_g001_a03_4224604e_002", "post_id": "jnofrxi", "subreddit": "GlobalTalk", "content": "I'm so sick of every discussion about the civilian death toll in Gaza turning into a debate over stats and reporting methods. It feels like people are actively looking for any tiny caveat just so they can ignore the actual human horror. Thousands of kids are dead, families are being wiped out, and millions have no food or water. Arguing over whether a headline is a 'perfect' comparison is just a giant cop-out. Why is it so hard for folks to just focus on the actual people who are suffering instead of playing scoreboard?"}
